    {
      "id": "de8b1b64-9f60-478f-930f-3d2c0b7b1764",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1120,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 848,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## Competitor price tracker\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Schedule Trigger fires every day at 08:00 AM.\n2. All monitored products are loaded from the DataTable and passed into a loop.\n3. For each product, ZenRows scrapes the retailer page and extracts the current price from JSON-LD structured data.\n4. The scraped price is compared against the stored value. The result \u2014 increase, decrease, stable, or error \u2014 is written back to the DataTable along with the updated price history.\n5. After the loop, only products with price changes pass through the filter.\n6. GPT-4.1-mini generates a plain-language alert listing each change with product name, old price, new price, and a direct link.\n7. The alert is sent to Telegram. Gmail is available as a disabled backup channel.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [x] Open Schedule Trigger and set your preferred execution hour.\n- [ ] Verify the DataTable node points to your product table and all required columns exist.\n- [ ] In set input data, replace {ZENROWS_API_KEY} with your live key from zenrows.com.\n- [ ] Connect your OpenAI API credential to the OpenAI Chat Model node.\n- [ ] Connect your Telegram Bot credential and set the Chat ID in Send a text message.\n- [ ] Optionally enable Send a message and connect Gmail OAuth2 for email backup.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the trigger hour in Schedule Trigger. Edit the system prompt in Summary writer to adjust the alert format or language."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
